      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There's Material.GetTags: (https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Material.GetTag.html) which can read some arbitrary data inside shaders. I bet if we did some tags like `\"VRCFallback\" = \"Toon\"`, we could have very fine control; and this same method could open up some interesting pathways for other shader data binding adventures. I can do a quick demo if it's needed.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
