      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I had to hammer this theory in longer with tests and some confirms to make this statement.\n\nThe shader fallback conditions are bad. It forces shaders to update to its standard and abandon its material variable saves in worst cases to adopt. It should of been a string check.\nEx, The system) \"An attempt is made to transfer parameters named \"_MainTex\" and \"_Color\" to the fallback shader/\"\n \nI went to review why i got so confused thinking i could never rename the String portion and got mixed up realizing the fallback system only looks for the Var name portion. This is bad because, like how we realized materials save keywords along with property name types,  materials will never lose saved settings if the var names stay the same and the string changes. These variable saves should be respected.\n\nIn my case renaming vars in my fork of UTS2 to be compatible with fallback caused the the proper \"_Color\" and the proper \"_Maintex\" variable names to not be backwards compatible at its worst differences. A user with whatever Booth pm model they had with whatever other persons version of the shader needs to manually understand how to do the conversion themselves by bring the different variable properties over in the debug material settings. This is trivial for me but not for a newb.\n\nThe fallback system should change to a sting lookup. Then first string match of main texture and color becomes the swap over. Organization guarantees matching name sets will come first.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
