      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a69eccdd20e79665351e7c1|full_name}: We're talking about the VRC Fallback system for when your shaders get blocked - not the built in Unity fallback.\n\nCurrently it searches for properties or parts of the shader name with strings comparisons, and falls back to a determined shader. \n\nSometimes this isn't really a viable solution, and it would be nice to specify which VRCFallback to use.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
